  "work": {
    "abstract_text": "Extending Mwafise's five-cycle example (26 October 2026, v1.0.0, README §4.4), we answer Problem 6.11 of Cheon, Jung, Kitaev and Mojallal, Riordan graphs II: Spectral properties, arXiv:1801.07021v1 (2018), p. 25, negatively: G_5(1+z^3,z(1+z^3)) is C_5 with inertia (3,2,0). The construction G_n(1+z^{n-2},z(1+z^{n-2}))=C_n yields counterexamples at every order 4q+1>=5. We prove minimality among all simple graphs, extend their even-series criterion to a finite-prefix characterization of bipartiteness for proper Bell-type graphs, and show that their absolute inertia bound is sharp at every order n>=2.",
